cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "sleep_scoring: An interactive desktop application for rodent EEG/EMG sleep scoring with optional deep-learning-assisted prediction"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Yue
    family-names: Zhao
    affiliation: "University of Rochester, Rochester, NY, USA"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-5012"
abstract: >-
  An open-source desktop application for visualizing, manually annotating, and
  automatically scoring rodent sleep stages from electroencephalogram (EEG),
  electromyogram (EMG), and optional fiber-photometry norepinephrine (NE)
  recordings. The app loads MATLAB .mat recordings, presents a synchronized
  interactive view of the EEG spectrogram, raw traces, and existing sleep
  scores, and lets a scorer label segments as Wake, Slow-Wave Sleep, or REM
  with keyboard shortcuts and aligned video. With the optional PyTorch
  dependency installed, a built-in transformer model (sDREAMER) scores a
  recording automatically for review and correction in the same interface.
  Annotations are written back into the original .mat file, and per-bout and
  per-stage summary statistics are exported to Excel.
repository-code: "https://github.com/yzhaoinuw/sleep_scoring"
license: MIT
version: 0.17.0
date-released: "2026-07-29"
keywords:
  - sleep scoring
  - electroencephalography
  - EEG
  - EMG
  - rodent
  - neuroscience
  - deep learning
  - annotation
  - norepinephrine
